      "created_at": "2015-01-18T15:02:54.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"xThe Killswitch\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n xThe Killswitch:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I'm so used to trading card games where destruction effects occurs in the graveyard, and I want to rule it the same way you did, Rabit. But then you have hairy cases where cards are \"not considered in play\" and it's just easier the way SotM handles these things.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Totally agree. My issue is predominantly the \"first learned\" problem, where something we learn later turns out to be wrong but we can't get it out of our heads. And it's especially hard to recognize when I'm tired.</p>",
